From b61857eaaebe438439462c1b234b819b76b4e43b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 23:38:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Client: ESBT is the engine; Loro and Yjs engines removed
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EsbtEngine keeps the loro-engine shape — IndexedDB warm open, shallow HTTP
snapshot, one WebSocket with a version vector on the URL, reconnect
backoff, deletion close code — on the @marks/esbt replica, with per-peer
undo grouped over a 500 ms window. Remote carets and selections move to a
new presence extension (collab/presence.ts) that publishes the contract's
${siteId}-cm-user / ${siteId}-cm-sel keys on a 15 s heartbeat and renders
peers as CodeMirror decorations, replacing loro-codemirror and
y-codemirror.next. Single-engine UI (no engine picker), legacy loro/yjs
rows are listed but refused with an explanation, and the benchmark page
now measures ESBT. loro-crdt, loro-codemirror, yjs, y-codemirror.next,
y-indexeddb and @hocuspocus/provider leave the dependency tree; the Vite
optimizeDeps exclusion for wasm-bindgen glue goes with them.
